# (scoped_class_scoped_call_prefix_identifier). This rule's intent is the
# scoped `<pkg>::<class>` prefix for a class_scope; the pkg slot MUST be a
# package, not a class. Without this predicate, PEG longest_match in the
# inner alternation of `class_scope_type` wrongly picks this branch for
# `C::m` (consuming `C::m` as `<pkg>::<class>`) over the SHORTER but
# CORRECT `known_unscoped_class_scope_class_identifier=C` branch; the
# subsequent mandatory `scope_resolution` in `class_scope` then fails
# (`C::m()` has only ONE `::`). Net: extern method body definitions like
# `function void C::m(); endfunction` were unparseable (the .b.6.2.12
# uvm_pkg blocker at lines 7651+ — uvm declares many method bodies
# externally via class::method qualifier). Adding `lacks_class` enforces
# the rule's true semantic.
