# SV-EXH-PROOF.3.3.4.b.6.2.12 — `class_scope_type` `*` loop guard
# (`&scope_resolution`). Pre-fix: the inner loop `( scope_resolution
# class_identifier ( pva )? )*` was greedy without a follow-on guard. For
# `C::m(...)` (where C is a class and m is a function_identifier in extern
# method body definition `function void C::m(); endfunction`), the loop
# wrongly consumed `::m` as another class-chain element, leaving no `::`
# for the OUTER `class_scope := class_scope_type scope_resolution`'s
# mandatory trailing `::`. Net: `class_scope` rejected `C::` whenever the
# next ident was followed by something other than `::`, so EVERY extern
# method body in uvm_pkg (lines 7651, 7660, 7668, 7676, 7688, ... — uvm
# heavily uses out-of-class method definitions) was unparseable. Adding
# `&scope_resolution` at the iteration tail ensures the loop only commits
# an iteration when ANOTHER `::` follows (matching the genuine deeper-
# chain form like `pkg::C::D::method`), leaving the FINAL `::method`
# correctly to the outer rule's trailing scope_resolution + the caller's
# function_identifier. Parser-AGNOSTIC level-0 grammar fix.
# SV-AST-SHAPE-FIDELITY.2.3 — named-lift of the class_scope_type head alternation so the
# bare `head: $1` in `class_scope_type` binds a clean named rule instead of an inline
# alternation (which corrupted the positional model → `params`/`scope_chain`
# `<invalid_sequence_access>` when the self-annotated `scoped_class_scope_identifier` branch
# won, e.g. `C::D::E`). The un-lifted twin of the already-correct `base_class_type` (`.2.2`
# `base_class_type_head`) / `class_type` (`class_type_head`) — same `{head, params,
# scope_chain}` shape; the `.1` `ansi_port_header` / `.2.1` `forward_type_keyword` precedent.
# The iteration tail (with its `&scope_resolution` lookahead) is unchanged.
class_scope_type_head := scoped_class_scope_identifier | known_unscoped_class_scope_class_identifier | known_unscoped_class_scope_interface_class_identifier | known_unscoped_class_scope_type_parameter_identifier

class_scope_type := class_scope_type_head ( parameter_value_assignment )? ( scope_resolution class_identifier ( parameter_value_assignment )? &scope_resolution )*
                 -> {head: $1, params: $2, scope_chain: $3}

@profiles: ["sv_2017", "sv_2023"]
class_scope := @probe_sample: "C::" class_scope_type scope_resolution
            -> {body: $1}

@predicate: { name: fact_attribute_equals, args: [type_name, $body, declaration_family, class], phase: post }
