# SV-EXH-PROOF.3.3.4.b.6.2.37.6 — per IEEE 1800 §A.8.3:
#   inside_expression ::= expression inside { open_range_list }
# The LRM has literal `{` and `}` braces around the range list. The prior
# pgen rule was `kw_inside open_range_list*` — MISSING the braces, and
# wrapped in `*` (zero-or-more) which made the rule match `inside` followed
# by nothing. Combined with the broken `value_range_sv_2017` (which also
# matched empty), this caused `inside {[1:5]}` to fail — the `{[1:5]}` was
# never recognised as the value list. Fix: require `lbrace ... rbrace`
# literally; `open_range_list` (one-or-more) consumes the list inside.
# Same fix shape for sv_2023's `range_list*`.
# Surfaced by `.37.5`'s 1,121,290 furthest reaching uvm_phase::jump's
# `phases.find(item) with (item.get_state() inside {[UVM_PHASE_STARTED:UVM_PHASE_CLEANUP]})`.
inside_expression_sv_2017 := expression_base kw_inside_fcc53788 lbrace open_range_list rbrace
                          -> {expr: $1, ranges: $4}

@profiles: ["sv_2023"]
inside_expression_sv_2023 := expression_base kw_inside_fcc53788 lbrace range_list rbrace
                          -> {expr: $1, ranges: $4}

