# BRANCH-PREDICATE-LOCALITY.2 (2026-07-06): the former third alternative
# (`hierarchical_tf_identifier -> {kind: "hierarchical", body: $1}`) is RETIRED
# deliberately. It had been dead since .b.6.2.2 landed: the branch-2 inline
# predicate was broadcast rule-wide by the engine's flattening bug and its
# `$scope.name.body` ref is unresolvable on a hierarchical result, so the branch
# was always predicate-killed (trace-proven; ledger/tree BRANCH-PREDICATE-LOCALITY §1b).
# With the engine fixed to the published branch-LOCAL contract, reviving the branch
# would have flipped statement-position and chain-initial dotted calls corpus-wide
# from the method-call carriers to `{kind:"tf"}` (measured on the reproducers) with
# zero correctness gain — identifier-headed hierarchical tf calls are carried by the
# method machinery, `$root.`-headed ones by `rooted_tf_call_sv_only` (the SV-0029
# lane), and this rule's contract is the SCOPED tf-name surface. Consequence, stated
# honestly: `hierarchical_tf_identifier`'s anchored (identifier-headed) alternative
# is now structurally unreachable — its only remaining consumer is
# `rooted_tf_call_sv_only`, whose `!( identifier )` firewall admits only `$root.`
# heads; it stays as documented LRM-faithful capacity for a future consumer.
# The @profiles tag is the linter's own derived minimal fix: with the hierarchical
# branch retired, both remaining branches reference class_scope/package_scope,
# which are absent under verilog_2005 (IEEE 1364-2005 has no classes/packages) —
# the rule was already runtime-dead there (branches 1-2 structurally unmatchable,
# branch 3 predicate-killed), so gating it is behavior-preserving (matrix-proven).
@profiles: ["sv_2017", "sv_2023"]
@branch_policy: priority_first
scoped_or_hierarchical_tf_identifier := class_scope tf_identifier                  -> {kind: "class_scope", scope: $1, name: $2}
                                      # .b.6.2.2: same $-ref defect as non_typedef_package_scope — drill via the branch's `scope: $1` (= package_scope = {kind, name: <package_identifier> = {body: scalar}}). Branch-LOCAL since BRANCH-PREDICATE-LOCALITY.2 (single evaluation, this branch only).
                                      | @predicate: { name: lacks_fact_attribute_equals, args: [type_name, $scope.name.body, declaration_family, typedef], phase: branch, view: shaped }
                                        package_scope tf_identifier                -> {kind: "package_scope", scope: $1, name: $2}

// @branch_policy: priority_first
// ps_or_hierarchical_tf_identifier := scoped_or_hierarchical_tf_identifier | tf_identifier

@predicate: { name: has_fact, args: [parameter_name, $body], phase: post }
