# SV-0066 (SV-CORPUS-GRAD.13c.2y): IEEE 1800-2017/2023 A.2.10 spells one property
# operator with the KEYWORD `implies`, and this grammar already had a rule of that
# name -- `implies := trivia "->"`, the ARROW. Extraction bound the keyword to it, so
# `a implies b` was unparseable while `a -> b` parsed as a property. SVA is
# SystemVerilog-only, so the token is profile-gated exactly like the `|->` / `|=>`
# pair SV-0039 added; IEEE 1364-2005 has no property_expr at all.
