# (SV-0030 fix, SV-DOLLAR-LRM-FIDELITY.3): the LRM scalar_constant / init_val digit
# alternatives had been prefix-merged into digit-less "1'b" / "1'B" tokens, so the
# IEEE spellings 1'b0 / 1'b1 / 1'B0 / 1'B1 REJECTED while the truncated "1'b" text
# ACCEPTED. The four digit-carrying tokens below restore the IEEE alternatives
# (regex \b so 1'b01 / 1'b0x are NOT prefix-stolen); the digit-less tokens were
# removed with their last referencing sites (init_val, scalar_constant).
#
# PGEN-SV-CORPUS-GRAD-0025 (.3.10, ledger SV-0046): the two `[ \t]*` seams admit
# LRM-legal white space INSIDE these literals. IEEE 1800-2017 section 5.7.1 (1364-2005
# section 3.5.1 identical) says a based literal "shall be composed of up to three
# tokens" — size / base_format / value — and then fixes exactly which of the two
# interior seams are open:
#   * size <-> apostrophe : OPEN. They are separate lexical tokens, so section 5.3
#     free-form separation applies and nothing carves it out.
#   * apostrophe <-> base char : CLOSED. "The apostrophe character and the base
#     format character shall not be separated by any white space." So `'B` / `'b`
#     stays contiguous below and `1' b 1` still REJECTS.
#   * base_format <-> value : OPEN, explicitly. "The unsigned number token shall
#     immediately follow the base format, optionally preceded by white space."
# This is the SAME law and the SAME `[ \t]*` idiom leaf .3.5 (ledger SV-0041) applied
# to integral_number:439 — but init_val / scalar_constant enumerate the LRM's CLOSED
# literal set, so they never route through integral_number and never inherited that
# fix. Keeping them as their own tokens (rather than swapping in integral_number)
# is what keeps the closed set closed: the leading `1` is hard-coded, so `2'b11`
# still cannot be an init_val. Additive — only previously-REJECTED spellings gain
# parses, and every emitted {kind:"1'b0"} ... {kind:"1'BX"} name is unchanged, so
# the locked ast_shape_contract samples (init_val_lrm_digits /
# scalar_constant_lrm_digits) hold and the AST schema does not move.
# `[ \t]` (horizontal) matches .3.5 deliberately; a literal spanning a NEWLINE is
# the same deferred composite-rule case there and here.
kw_n_1_tick_B0_720c4a9c := trivia /1[ \t]*'B[ \t]*0\b/

kw_n_1_tick_B1_afad66cc := trivia /1[ \t]*'B[ \t]*1\b/

kw_n_1_tick_BX_874bf116 := trivia /1[ \t]*'B[ \t]*X/

kw_n_1_tick_Bx_0a99de19 := trivia /1[ \t]*'B[ \t]*x/

kw_n_1_tick_b0_cc597d72 := trivia /1[ \t]*'b[ \t]*0\b/

kw_n_1_tick_b1_a5c2b78e := trivia /1[ \t]*'b[ \t]*1\b/

kw_n_1_tick_bX_70a6d618 := trivia /1[ \t]*'b[ \t]*X/

kw_n_1_tick_bx_ab9cb068 := trivia /1[ \t]*'b[ \t]*x/

kw_n_1step_e6d37e7c := trivia /1step\b/


