# (SV-0030 fix, SV-DOLLAR-LRM-FIDELITY.3): the unsized IEEE scalar_constant
# alternatives 'b0 / 'b1 / 'B0 / 'B1 (previously realized digit-less as
# `tick kw_b` / `tick kw_B`, accepting bare 'b / 'B).
#
# PGEN-SV-CORPUS-GRAD-0025 (.3.10, ledger SV-0046): the single `[ \t]*` seam is the
# IEEE 1800-2017 section 5.7.1 base_format <-> value allowance ("The unsigned number
# token shall immediately follow the base format, optionally preceded by white
# space"). These four are UNSIZED, so they have only ONE interior seam — there is no
# size token, hence no size<->apostrophe seam, and the apostrophe<->base-char seam is
# the one section 5.7.1 explicitly CLOSES. See the sized twins near kw_n_1_tick_B0
# for the full derivation.
kw_tick_B0_f33e35dd := trivia /'B[ \t]*0\b/

kw_tick_B1_230dd583 := trivia /'B[ \t]*1\b/

kw_tick_b0_624cb09b := trivia /'b[ \t]*0\b/

kw_tick_b1_1c5be368 := trivia /'b[ \t]*1\b/

kw_this_c2543fff := trivia /this\b/

kw_throughout_330dbf47 := trivia /throughout\b/

kw_time_714eea0f := trivia /time\b/

kw_timeprecision_628f1cfc := trivia /timeprecision\b/

kw_timeunit_57f78b2f := trivia /timeunit\b/

// kw_token_08534f33 := trivia /\\\b/

# (SV-CORPUS-GRAD.3.9 fix, ledger SV-0045): the fused literals
# `kw_token_71b8cf7e := trivia "##[*]"` and `kw_token_9768502a := trivia "##[+]"`
# were RETIRED here. Each fused FOUR distinct SystemVerilog lexical tokens
# (`##` + `[` + `*`/`+` + `]`) into one atom, and a fused multi-character literal
# cannot admit interior white space — but IEEE 1800-2017 §5.3 ignores white space
# "except when [it serves] to separate other lexical tokens", so every spaced
# spelling (`## [*]`, `##[ * ]`, ...) is legal SystemVerilog and ALL of them
# rejected. `cycle_delay_range` now spells both alternatives structurally out of
# the existing `kw_token_93ac8946` / `lbrack` / `star` / `plus` / `rbrack` tokens,
# exactly as `consecutive_repetition` (:1377) already does.
kw_token_93ac8946 := trivia "##"

